.El
.Pp
However it ends, an unanswered event is abandoned (design 8.2): one the
controller has not yet read is withdrawn silently; one already delivered
is marked interrupted and a
.Dv DQ_OP_INTERRUPT
record names it, so a deadline that expires after delivery posts the same
record a signal does
.Pq Va ds_interrupts counts the other cases .
When a reply and a signal race, the state decides: a reply that landed
first is consumed and no interruption is recorded.
.Pp
A
.Dv DQ_OP_LOCK
wait has no deadline, whatever the policy says: a blocked
.Dv F_SETLKW
is a legitimate wait of any length on a real file.
Lock waits are counted apart from the in-flight bounds (a blocked locker
never holds a slot readers and writers need) and bounded by the queue
depth alone; a signal ends one, with
.Dv DQ_OP_INTERRUPT .
.Dv DQ_OP_UNLOCK_ALL ,
.Dv DQ_OP_CLOSE
